    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let the number of bounces after which the ball raises less than $30$ cm be $n.$\n\nAfter the first bounce, the ball rises $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ centimeter. After the second bounce, the ball rises $\\dfrac{2}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{2}{3}=\\dfrac{2^2}{3^2}$ centimeters, after the third bounce, it rises $\\dfrac{2^3}{3^3}$ centimeters, and so on. The ball will rise less than $30$ cm after the $n$th bounce if $\\dfrac{2^n}{3^n} < 30.$ Another way to write this is $\\dfrac{2^n}{3^n} \\le 30$, then $\\dfrac{2^n}{3^n} > 30$. Since $n$ is a positive integer, $\\dfrac{2^n}{3^n} < 30$ is true for $n = 5$, and $\\dfrac{2^n}{3^n} > 30$ is true for $n = 6$.\n\n$n = \\boxed{6}$",
